※ A variable here lasts as long as the program, so what a lambda kept would
※ have to as well -- and what it kept belongs to the call that wrote it.  It is
※ the rule about answering with one, asked at the other place a value can
※ escape to.

let kept: fn(u8) → u8 = ⊥

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
